{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1785185481,"nonce":"yqvevpHYsaDsZ9e5WNSIhu/hCZc=","title":"ADR-0062: the overlay change-set integration test has never executed its assertions","message":"A test tier that can actually run `crates/scarab-server/tests/changeset_overlay.rs`.\n\nThe test is correctly written and correctly gated: `#[ignore]` plus `SCARAB_TEST_OVERLAY=1`, and once opted in **every** unmet precondition panics rather than returning — non-Linux, missing `SCARAB_TEST_OVERLAY_DIR`, missing `CAP_SYS_ADMIN`, failed mount. That is the right shape and it is the fix for the class of bug repaired at commit `505f313`, where seven live tests reported PASS while executing nothing.\n\n**But the mount-and-assert bodies have never run**, because there is no privileged Linux host with a Rust toolchain in the loop. The expected values are not invented — they are the twelve entries a privileged probe container produced on kernel 6.8.0 (whiteouts as `c--------- 0, 0`; `opaque=\"y\"`; `origin` on copied-up files; `impure`+`origin` on their parents; a file rename as whiteout-plus-copy with no redirect; a directory rename under `redirect_dir=on` as `redirect=\"olddir\"` plus whiteout). So the assertions encode measurement. They have still never been executed by the harness, and an assertion that has never run is not yet a test.\n\nOptions, in rough order of cost: run the crate's tests inside a privileged container on the existing colima cluster; add it to the `kind` tier that already exists for live tests; or a GitHub Actions Linux job (blocked while Actions is quota-blocked account-wide).\n\n\n- [ ] The mount-and-assert bodies execute somewhere reproducible, driven by a `just` recipe\n- [ ] Each assertion is shown to fail when the code under test is mutated — the mutations exist and are listed in the slice's report, but were only run against the pure classifier\n- [ ] The recipe fails loudly when the tier is opted in and unavailable; it must never report success having skipped\n- [ ] Documented which kernel and filesystem the run covered, since every value here is kernel-version-dependent\n\n\n- cb53ca9 (s2) landing first","files":null}]}